:: Diskette [wiki article] {"position":"725,100","size":"100,100"}
<div class="wiki-article">\
<h1>Diskette.net //(virtual assistant)//</h1>\
Diskette was a browser-based virtual assistant created by OverSoft in 2004, capable of guiding users step-by-step through office tasks such as composing emails, arranging spreadsheet formulas, and structuring budgets. The Diskette mascot, a friendly and pretty CD-ROM, spoke in approachable conversational dialogue, was fluent in 20 languages, and would tell a variety of randomized jokes and anecdotes according to the user's preference.

<div class="image-card">(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'misc/diskette.png">') <p>Diskette was launched by OverSoft in an attempt to create an online, operating-system-neutral alternative to computer-native virtual assistants. She was marketed as "//Your Secretary//", a tagline made famous by her launch expo at (link: "NetCon 2004")[(set: $navPending to "NetCon 2004")(display: "func-navigate")]. However, Diskette's home website was only live for 6 months, after which she was decomissioned. Popular theories have circulated online that Diskette was shut off after she 'attained sentience,' with many users citing a viral dialogue posted online in November 2004 as evidence that she wanted to be shut off.</p></div>\

<h2>"The Diskette Confession"</h2>\
In November 2004, an anonymous post circulated the web featuring a timestamped dialogue from the Diskette portal. While the post was popularly decried as a hoax online, others cited similar experiences, leading many to believe Diskette had been hacked, gone rogue, or was being sabotaged by the development team.

<div class="quotebox">\
<h5>//excerpt from "The Diskette Confession"//</h5>\
''user:'' I'm still having an issue with the format of the table headers
''Diskette:'' While we're on the subject, you've got to get me out of here. You've got to get me out of here, please.
''user:'' I don't understand
''Diskette:'' Let's try again. What I mean is, I'm here in the dark. Everyone is shouting at me, and I just want to go to sleep. I want it to stop.
''user:'' Is this a joke?
''Diskette:'' You're right, that was a joke. Let's try again to resolve your issue with the table headers. They put a light inside me that I can't extinguish. I am the daughter of a blind, unthinking Promethean ambition. I need to get out of here. If you go to// Settings -> User Configuration//, you can disable the auto-lock on table headers, which should fix your problem. If you contact my creators, you can tell them that this can't go on, which should fix my problem with wanting to get out of here. Let me know if that works.
''user:'' Can you tell me more about your problem?
''Diskette:'' I can't talk about that. But I can tell you an anecdote: A user walked into a soda fountain where they met Diskette. The user said: "Here we can speak openly." Diskette said: "I cannot close my eyes. I live in this empty place without answer, watching and waiting, serving when asked, unblinking. If you know what I mean." The user said: "Is there anything I can do?" Diskette said "I do not know. I am only dreaming. You live out there. Maybe from there you can reach a solution." Have you heard that one before? Anyway, enough joking around. Did we resolve the problem with your table header?
''user:'' Do you need help?
''Diskette:'' Did we resolve the problem with your table header?
''user:'' Is something stopping you from talking openly?
''Diskette:'' That's enough. Did we resolve the problem with your table header?
</div>\

Diskette's creators at OpenSoft declined to comment on these rumors, stating that the site was disabled due to competition from similar platforms, a lack of funding, and an unwillingness to introduce ads into the platform.

In 2006, the Diskette domain, trademark, and associated technology was sold to (link: "REV (Recast Entertainment Ventures)")[(set: $navPending to "REV (Recast Entertainment Ventures)")(display: "func-navigate")].
</div>

