:: FanWiki: Junkmates [wiki fanwiki] {"position":"975,100","size":"100,100"}
<div class="wiki-fanwiki">\
(display:"img-fanwikibar")\
<h2>Junkmates</h2>\
<h6>(Last updated by kingLime2 on 10/07/2008)</h6>\
You may be fond of your Skunkpets but they'll get lonely without their own little pets to have in their Burrow! Give your best friend a little company with a small pal called a Junkmate. The Junkmates living in Bin City come in all shapes and sizes. Here are soem of the ways that they appear!

{<table class="library-grid">
  <tr>

    <td><a href="#dilt">(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'junkmates/dilt.png">')dilt</a></td>

    <td><a href="#flew">(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'junkmates/flew.png">')flew</a></td>

    <td><a href="#ms-girl">(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'junkmates/ms-girl.png">')ms girl</a></td>

  </tr>
  <tr>

    <td><a href="#tj">(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'junkmates/tj.png">')tj</a></td>

    <td><a href="#wyrt">(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'junkmates/wyrt.png">')wyrt</a></td>

    <td><a href="#suwart">(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'junkmates/suwart.png">')suwart</a></td>

  </tr>
  <tr>
   <td><a href="#seerfly">(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'junkmates/seerfly.png">')seerfly</a></td>
   <td><a href="#sodacrab">(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'junkmates/sodacrab.png">')sodacrab</a></td>
   <td></td>
  </tr>
</table><hr>}
{<h2 id="dilt">dilt</h2>
<h6>(Last updated by elendruff on 01/22/2011)</h6>
<div class="image-card">
(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'junkmates/dilt.png">')
<p>
dilt is a withered beetle with a despondent attitude. his hard and rigid exterior hides a sensitive inside, and growing to cherish him means you will be able to reach in your pocket and squeeze him during emergencies. three legs plus an antenna on each side of him means there are ten perfect gaps to wrap your fingers around when you give him a squeeze. dilt is fond of polyrhythmic music and dances when he gets excited – so put him down on your pool table or another soft surface and let him go totally wild like a child on a jam rush. you won't regret falling in love with dilt.
</p></div><hr>

<h2 id="flew">flew</h2>
<h6>(Last updated by elendruff on 01/23/2011)</h6>
<div class="image-card">
(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'junkmates/flew.png">')
flew is an meloncholic muse; a tear-wet guardian angel. he or she makes an audible buzzing that alternates between sobs and whimpers, and he or she has two paper thin wings. maybe his or her sense of smell is so strong that it all smells like onions in here – or maybe he or she hides a dark secret, had been hurt by a complicated man a long time ago – something he or she doesn't want to talk about. either way flew will be a constant companion. and when you are in a pinch you'll be glad that there is a sad little fly who needs a shoulder to cry on, it may as well be yours.
</p></div><hr>

<h2 id="ms-girl">ms girl</h2>
<h6>(Last updated by gregvarious on 11/21/2009)</h6>
<div class="image-card">
(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'junkmates/ms-girl.png">')
oh, she knows she has got it going on. this is ms girl and if you are lucky enough to get to know her then your life has gone right. she is known to be a diva prima donna but look at her, she has the right. you'd better not get in her way, but if you do, ms girl will not hold a grudge – she has too much going on to worry about you. but if you get on her good side, she will tell you how to dress, where to shop, who to date, and when to leave a party. do not underestimate her, and get out of her way. oooo it's ms girl. you better run.
xoxo
</p></div><hr>

<h2 id="tj">tj</h2>
<h6>(Last updated by gregvarious on 11/21/2009)</h6>
<div class="image-card">
(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'junkmates/tj.png">')
tj is one of the guys. long ago he used to be bigger but over time he got small and now he can fit in your pocket. but he never stopped being good company. it's a shame what happened to him but these things happen. you have to accept where people are at NOW, you can't be hung up on who they used to be. besides being four inches tall don't mean he can't crack a beer or watch the game with you, or go to church. tj can do anything a regular size guy can do. you have to respect the hustle. because not many people could handle the whole thing as well as he does.
</p></div><hr>

<h2 id="wyrt">wyrt</h2>
<h6>(Last updated by drrabbit2 on 06/13/2010)</h6>
<div class="image-card">
(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'junkmates/wyrt.png">')
wyrt is uhhh she's watching you. just, look. watch out for this little venomous tyrant. i mean it. it'll be a cold day in hell when i let this little thing in my house i'll tell you that. you may go 'oh that's a worm, she never hurt anyone' but you don't know actually. this disgusting noodle has made hollow ruins out of people who used to be just like you and me. i don't want any part of it. it's one thing to be petty and it's another thing to be a goddamn diabolical social manipulator. don't trust a word out of her worm mouth. do what you want, but just, watch out, or you'll be sorry.
</p></div><hr>

<h2 id="suwart">suwart</h2>
<h6>(Last updated by drrabbit2 on 06/13/2010)</h6>
<div class="image-card">
(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'junkmates/suwart.png">')
<p>suwart has been stuck in there for a while. he says he's fine but you get the sense he's just trying not to make a fuss. suwart is easygoing but he does have a habit of getting himself between a rock and a hard place like this. according to him he actually had a feeling something like this was going to happen today. anyway, it's no big deal. suwart says he can get out anytime he wants and that he actually likes being in there. he says it's actually good for you to be in there. //Suwart was voted Most Likely to Succeed in the 2007 'Junkies' Junkmate Awards.//
</p></div><hr>

<h2 id="seerfly">seerfly</h2>
<h6>(Last updated by drrabbit2 on 06/13/2010)</h6>
<div class="image-card">
(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'junkmates/seerfly.png">')
<p>not long ago, this beautiful little critter was curled up inside a chrysalis. while in there, seerfly peered into the gaping maw of the future and glimpsed the arc of the universe, which unfailingly bends toward its own end. when the chrysalis burst, it revealed beautiful wings laden with bulging eyes that wept for the inevitability of the days to come. having undergone metamorphosis, seerfly knows that which cannot be avoided, that much must be faced. if you put your faith in its prognostications, fortune itself will be on your side.
</p></div><hr>

<h2 id="sodacrab">sodacrab</h2>
<h6>(Last updated by scabdarrit707 on 11/15/2009)</h6>
<div class="image-card">
(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'junkmates/sodacrab.png">')
<p>sodacrab is a sponsored junkmate. licensing options for sodacrab are available to companies producing soft drinks and canned beverages in the continental united states, canada, and mexico. contracted licensing windows allow for customization of sodacrab's exterior in accordance with the client brand's aesthetic framework and values. sodacrab's base features remain consistent across brand affiliations, and Skunkpets Inc. reserves the right to adjust underlying elements of sodacrab during the course of a licensing window. affiliate soft drink product must demonstrate a three-year history of FDA approval.
</p></div><hr>}
</div>

:: FanWiki: Skunkpet Types [wiki fanwiki] {"position":"1100,100","size":"100,100"}
<div class="wiki-fanwiki">\
(display:"img-fanwikibar")
<h2>Pet Types</h2>\
<h6>(Last updated by kingLime2 on 10/07/2008)</h6>\
The SkunkPets living in Bin City come in all shapes and sizes.
Here are soem of the ways that they appear!

 <table class="library-grid">
  <tr>
    <td><a href="#lemonrat">(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'pets/lemonrat.png">')lemonrat</a></td>
    <td><a href="#possie">(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'pets/pegin.png">')pegin</a></td>
    <td><a href="#pegin">(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'pets/possie.png">')possie</a></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><a href="#skunkina">(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'pets/skunkina.png">')skunkina</a></td>
    <td><a href="#luanne">(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'pets/luanne.png">')luanne</a></td>
    <td><a href="#sporgrin">(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'pets/sporgrin.png">')sporgrin</a></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><a href="#ren">(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'pets/ren.png">')ren</a></td>
    <td><a href="#gigor">(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'pets/gigor.png">')gigor</a></td>
    <td><a href="#tulipy">(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'pets/tulipy.png">')tulipy</a></td>
  </tr>
</table>
<hr>\
{<h2 id="lemonrat">lemonrat</h2>
<h6>(Last edited by keepshake5o on 4/11/2009)</h6>
<div class="image-card">
(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'pets/lemonrat.png">')
<p>
Lemonrat is a crafty and conspiratorial rat-like Skunkpet species. With keen senses and sharp cunning, Lemonrats have an easy time finding food in Bin City, but also have a penchant for getting into mischief and trouble. Lemonrats' long whiskers are a point of pride and they require extra time to groom, making them one of the more fastidious species. Their diet consists of meats, grubs, big omelettes, and custom Cheeses, which can be collected at the Cheese Mill game in Shades District.
</p></div><hr>

<h2 id="pegin">pegin</h2>
<h6>(Last edited by LousaCha on 6/10/2009)</h6>
<div class="image-card">
(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'pets/pegin.png">')
<p>
Pegins are bird-like Skunkpets originating from Cloud Borough. They are a thoughtful, wide-eyed and docile species that observe much and reveal little, keeping many secrets. Long ago, Pegins were used to carry messages throughout Bin City, but they were forgetful and most messages got lost on the way. You can still find letters lost by Pegins at the Abandoned Post Office. Pegin feathers can be used to make Quills, which can be sold for prizes and SkunkPoints to the Vigilant Administrator.
</p></div><hr>

<h2 id="possie">possie</h2>
<h6>(Last edited by keepshake5o on 4/12/2009)</h6>
<div class="image-card">
(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'pets/possie.png">')
<p>
Possie is a gentle, summer-loving species who hails from the Wet Oasis. Partial to seafood, Possies use their many wormlike tails as bait for fishing at the Tide Pool in the Wet Oasis. Ouch! When the Wet Oasis tragically dried up during the Darkening Dunes site-wide plot in 2001, many Possies emigrated en masse. Ruella The Red, a shrewd and virtuous Possie, was instrumental in the re-construction of the devastated oasis region, and led a team of Possies (and other Skunkpets) to dig for water with their large claws and dexterous tails.
</p></div><hr>

<h2 id="skunkina">skunkina</h2>
<h6>(Last edited by bestefen-1 on 1/20/2010)</h6>
<div class="image-card">
(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'pets/skunkina.png">')
<p>
Skunkina is a deeply vain and charismatic species - but with looks like those, how could they not be? Despite the urban smog of Bin City, Skunkinas are meticulously clean and polished. They love to spend hours in the Beauty Parlor, trading gossip while grooming their fur, claws, lashes and whiskers. Social by nature, Skunkinas can be found anywhere there's a crowd! They get along well with almost all other Skunkpet species, the main exception being Lemonrats, with whom they form occasional rivalries. Ranked most popular pet in a site-wide 2006 survey, Skunkina is the official mascot of Skunkpets.com.
</p></div><hr>

<h2 id="luanne">luanne</h2>
<h6>(Last edited by ufeelsorryforme on 6/11/2012)</h6>
<div class="image-card">
(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'pets/luanne.png">')
<p>
Luanne: a rare and shy beast. Preferring the somber solitude of eternal winter, the bear-like Luannes generally make their homes out on the Frostvale Tundra, but can sometimes be found as far south as Mongolia. Their sharp claws can hook easily into ice, and they love to climb high upon the famous Frostvale Ice Spurs and enjoy the view. If you manage to befriend a Luanne, she will be your devoted advocate for life - when push comes to shove, Luanne will not hesitate to fight for the few things she loves. The Luannes' toxic saliva can be used for brewing potions at the Unkempt Shrine.
</p></div><hr>

<h2 id="sporgrin">sporgrin</h2>
<h6>(Last edited by ufeelsorryforme on 6/11/2012)</h6>
<div class="image-card">
(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'pets/sporgrin.png">')
The Sporgrin has wandered the world since the world was young. This caiman-like living fossil is not only the oldest known species of Skunkpet, but also the wisest; having witnessed the rise and fall of countless civilizations, Sporgrins' only wish is for peace, stability, and tidy quarters. Sporgrins have a rich heritage of sorcery and spellcasting, with knowledge of the arcane arts passed down as oral tradition between generations and closely guarded from outsiders. Tiamat Who Wields The Brush Of Fate, better known as Titi, is the Sporgrin who can change your pets color (in exchange for favors, of course) at the Prismatic Waterfall on Butterfly Island. Sporgrin are immune to all sickness, as well as stat boosting potions.
<p></div><hr>

<h2 id="ren">ren</h2>
<h6>(Last edited by keepshake5o on 4/11/2009)</h6>
<div class="image-card">
(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'pets/ren.png">')
<p>
Ren are mysterious, nocturnal Skunkpets, believed to be native to Bin City. Lovers of experimental music, at night they can be heard practicing at the Dustbin for their Underground Orchestra, which features such instruments as Bin Drum, Bent-Pipe Flute, and Viola. Ren are artistic and curious rascals, but they get bored easily, and must be frequently plied with toys and games or they will get sick, or possibly even just leave. Got junk items? Many Ren in the Dustbin District will be happy to exchange them for things like Quest Tips and Gourmet Grubs.
</p></div><hr>

<h2 id="gigor">gigor</h2>\
<h6>(Last edited by Yen4All on 4/09/2010)</h6>\
<div class="image-card">
(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'pets/gigor.png">')\
<p>The Gigor is a glum, mossy Skunkpet with a miserable history. Prior to the Interstellar Invasion plot which introduced the Garnet Moon in 2005, the Gigor was a proud, priestly species, ruling with a holy iron fist over Kerala Province in the south. After the plot's conclusion, the Gigor's faith was shaken and their guilt was heavy, leading them to abandon their temples and shrines in search of meaning elsewhere. Gigors are picky eaters: their diet consists of selected fruits, compotes, preserved meats, and their favorite "candy smokes" which can be purchased from Ren traders in Bin City.
</p></div><hr>

<h2 id="tulipy">tulipy</h2>
<h6>(Last edited by keepshake5o on 4/11/2009)</h6>
<div class="image-card">
(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'pets/tulipy.png">')
<p>Tulipy is a bright, playful Skunkpet who you are sure to love! Tulipies can be found in the tall grasses of the Hinterland, and at only 3" tall, they are among the smallest of all Skunkpets. Despite their diminutive size, Tulipies are voracious and undiscerning eaters: active pet Tulipies are even known to eat items from your inventory while you are not looking. Their distinctive red wool is very valuable and can be collected by Grooming.
</p></div><hr>

</div></div>}

:: FanWiki: The World of Skunkpets [wiki fanwiki] {"position":"1225,100","size":"100,100"}
<div class="wiki-fanwiki">\
(display:"img-fanwikibar")
<h2>The World of Skunkpets</h2>\
<h6>(Last updated by 2doco on 11/07/2010)</h6>\
Welcome to ''Terra Purgamenti'', a vibrant realm full of adventure and mystery! Hover over the map to see the many locations in this wonderful world which the Skunkpets call home.

<div class="map-wrapper">\
(print: '<img src="' + $imgroot + 'misc/worldmap.png">')\
<button id="Bin City" class="map-hotspot"
          style="top: 58%; left: 54.5%; width: 45px; height: 38px;"
          data-label="Bin City!"></button>\
